8050
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:09,530
Like being in a dreamland

9790
00:00:09,790 --> 00:00:11,343
Magical powers gifted to me

11703
00:00:11,703 --> 00:00:13,470
From a pocket full of treasures

15843
00:00:15,843 --> 00:00:17,363
Traveling together across infinite space

17630
00:00:17,630 --> 00:00:19,289
Catching atop the Milky Way

19403
00:00:19,403 --> 00:00:21,496
The beauty of time

23416
00:00:23,416 --> 00:00:25,163
Whenever we run into trouble

25383
00:00:25,383 --> 00:00:30,256
Transforming anytime, anywhere with flashes of inspiration

30669
00:00:30,669 --> 00:00:33,023
Quickly flying to a carefree wonderland

33173
00:00:33,173 --> 00:00:34,973
Hand in hand with starlight

34998
00:00:34,998 --> 00:00:37,695
Sparkling and dancing

39076
00:00:39,076 --> 00:00:42,636
Stepping through this door whenever we like

42910
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:46,590
Making our hopes real and dreams come true

46990
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:50,617
Crossing railways and countryside

50790
00:00:50,790 --> 00:00:54,357
In a flash, the dream express appears again

54717
00:00:54,717 --> 00:00:55,903
Sha-la-la-la-la

56090
00:00:56,090 --> 00:00:58,510
Singing along with me

58717
00:00:58,717 --> 00:00:59,943
Calling out for an encore

60043
00:01:00,043 --> 00:01:02,509
Marching together in fun

62563
00:01:02,563 --> 00:01:03,790
Doraemon

63903
00:01:03,903 --> 00:01:05,836
Keeping this moment timeless

65863
00:01:05,863 --> 00:01:09,910
Our dreams will finally come true

70290
00:01:10,290 --> 00:01:11,530
Sha-la-la-la-la

71710
00:01:11,710 --> 00:01:13,943
Singing along with me

74283
00:01:14,283 --> 00:01:15,483
Calling out for an encore

75790
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:18,080
Marching together in fun

78234
00:01:18,234 --> 00:01:19,467
Doraemon

79534
00:01:19,534 --> 00:01:21,474
Keeping this moment timeless

81527
00:01:21,527 --> 00:01:28,860
Beautiful sights will surely be seen

91325
00:01:31,325 --> 00:01:34,018
"What Kind of Day Is Halloween?"

101165
00:01:41,165 --> 00:01:42,371
What on earth is that?

107236
00:01:47,236 --> 00:01:48,091
Nobita!

108131
00:01:48,131 --> 00:01:49,951
Are you all right, Nobita?

111266
00:01:51,266 --> 00:01:52,383
A monster!

112424
00:01:52,424 --> 00:01:54,331
- Trick or treat!
- Trick or treat!

114680
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:57,197
Oh right, today is Halloween!

117238
00:01:57,238 --> 00:01:58,219
Halloween?

118260
00:01:58,260 --> 00:02:00,915
It's a holiday celebrating the autumn harvest

120956
00:02:00,956 --> 00:02:02,955
Kids dress up like monsters

122995
00:02:02,995 --> 00:02:05,413
and go around to neighbors' houses to get candy

125539
00:02:05,539 --> 00:02:08,145
And they also say "trick or treat"

128186
00:02:08,186 --> 00:02:09,625
They say "trick or treat"?

130234
00:02:10,234 --> 00:02:13,434
It means if you don't give them a treat, they'll play a trick on you

134200
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,882
If you dress like a monster and say that, you get candy?

136948
00:02:16,948 --> 00:02:19,511
Since we have the chance, can we give it a try?

139552
00:02:19,552 --> 00:02:21,412
Sure, let's try it...

141482
00:02:21,482 --> 00:02:23,402
Yeah, seems like fun!

143616
00:02:23,616 --> 00:02:26,088
Let's dress up as monsters and meet at the open lot!

148530
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:29,730
Trick... uh...

149890
00:02:29,890 --> 00:02:31,217
Sa...

151683
00:02:31,683 --> 00:02:33,441
What are you muttering to yourself for?

153482
00:02:33,482 --> 00:02:35,164
Today is Halloween, you know

155674
00:02:35,674 --> 00:02:37,463
If you dress like a monster, you get candy to eat

157503
00:02:37,503 --> 00:02:38,689
For free?

158960
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,284
You just have to say the magic words

160325
00:02:40,325 --> 00:02:41,189
Magic words?

161571
00:02:41,571 --> 00:02:43,184
Tr...

163358
00:02:43,358 --> 00:02:44,233
Ah, right!

164273
00:02:44,273 --> 00:02:46,527
"Sake bottle or treatment!"

166944
00:02:46,944 --> 00:02:48,608
A sake bottle would be nice, though...

168649
00:02:48,649 --> 00:02:51,059
But a treatment is hard to pass up too

172798
00:02:52,798 --> 00:02:54,305
Is that how it goes?

174411
00:02:54,411 --> 00:02:55,915
So that's how it is

175995
00:02:55,995 --> 00:02:57,296
Even though I don't know

177336
00:02:57,336 --> 00:02:59,326
what kind of holiday Halloween is

179476
00:02:59,476 --> 00:03:01,476
if you can get stuff from people

181516
00:03:01,516 --> 00:03:03,167
it must be a great holiday

183997
00:03:03,997 --> 00:03:05,096
Thanks a lot

186850
00:03:06,850 --> 00:03:08,490
Don't mention it

193438
00:03:13,438 --> 00:03:15,279
Why did you dress up like that?

196838
00:03:16,838 --> 00:03:20,300
Western knights are for Halloween costumes

201279
00:03:21,279 --> 00:03:24,399
Looking like that isn't Halloween, it's Children's Day!

204440
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:26,678
Details like that don't matter

206761
00:03:26,761 --> 00:03:29,362
Doraemon, join in too, let's head to the empty lot!

209402
00:03:29,402 --> 00:03:30,172
Sure

210890
00:03:30,890 --> 00:03:32,942
Dekisugi, your costume is great!

212983
00:03:32,983 --> 00:03:35,903
Shizuka, your witch costume looks so real

215979
00:03:35,979 --> 00:03:37,136
Really?

217177
00:03:37,177 --> 00:03:38,994
Have you two been waiting long?

219925
00:03:39,925 --> 00:03:42,370
Doesn't my costume look great?

222810
00:03:42,810 --> 00:03:45,783
You're asking if it's good? How should I put this...

225923
00:03:45,923 --> 00:03:47,407
Very unique taste

227447
00:03:47,447 --> 00:03:48,563
Exactly

231489
00:03:51,489 --> 00:03:53,368
If you don't have money, it's so uncomfortable

235691
00:03:55,691 --> 00:03:58,158
Speaking of rich people, of course it's a king

239352
00:03:59,352 --> 00:04:01,264
His Majesty is heading out

242991
00:04:02,991 --> 00:04:04,391
Huh? What's going on?

246350
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:09,005
I am the great thief Ishikawa Goemon

249703
00:04:09,703 --> 00:04:13,416
"Sake bottle or treatment!"

254979
00:04:14,979 --> 00:04:16,736
Uh... Gian, what are you doing?

256884
00:04:16,884 --> 00:04:19,813
If you don't give me toys, I'll play a trick on you!

260664
00:04:20,664 --> 00:04:21,367
Come on

261427
00:04:21,427 --> 00:04:23,961
Which one do you choose? Tell me

269896
00:04:29,896 --> 00:04:32,127
Which house should we go to next?

275008
00:04:35,008 --> 00:04:37,023
- Trick or treat!
- Trick or treat!

278092
00:04:38,092 --> 00:04:39,422
Here, take these

281409
00:04:41,409 --> 00:04:42,801
Thank you so much!

285877
00:04:45,877 --> 00:04:47,583
It's so sweet and delicious

287624
00:04:47,624 --> 00:04:48,842
I'm so happy

288882
00:04:48,882 --> 00:04:50,935
Halloween is really great

292332
00:04:52,332 --> 00:04:54,391
Suneo never showed up in the end

294432
00:04:54,432 --> 00:04:56,305
He was so excited about it before

296377
00:04:56,377 --> 00:04:58,298
S-Sake bottle...

298338
00:04:58,338 --> 00:05:00,517
Sake Bottle Gian!

304636
00:05:04,636 --> 00:05:06,117
He said Halloween is a day

306158
00:05:06,158 --> 00:05:08,449
where you can demand whatever you want from people

308497
00:05:08,497 --> 00:05:10,304
No, he's got it all wrong!

310352
00:05:10,352 --> 00:05:11,784
Oh, could it be...

311897
00:05:11,897 --> 00:05:13,021
What's going on?

313168
00:05:13,168 --> 00:05:14,088
Hey

315261
00:05:15,261 --> 00:05:16,124
Gian!

316222
00:05:16,222 --> 00:05:17,211
Nobita

317282
00:05:17,282 --> 00:05:20,363
Thanks a lot for explaining it so clearly to me earlier

321406
00:05:21,406 --> 00:05:23,255
You've got it wrong, Gian

323328
00:05:23,328 --> 00:05:24,788
Halloween is...

324888
00:05:24,888 --> 00:05:26,669
You guys hurry home and wait for me

326709
00:05:26,709 --> 00:05:28,439
I'll be visiting each of you in a bit

332057
00:05:32,057 --> 00:05:33,235
Nobita

333276
00:05:33,276 --> 00:05:35,222
what on earth did you say to Gian?

336548
00:05:36,548 --> 00:05:38,528
Doraemon, think of something!

338569
00:05:38,569 --> 00:05:40,748
You tell me to think of something, but what can I do?

340789
00:05:40,789 --> 00:05:41,863
If this keeps up

341903
00:05:41,903 --> 00:05:43,644
The consequences will be terrible

345780
00:05:45,780 --> 00:05:47,111
There's that gadget!

349488
00:05:49,488 --> 00:05:51,263
"Jack-o'-Lantern"

352586
00:05:52,586 --> 00:05:53,986
Everyone, hurry home

354026
00:05:54,026 --> 00:05:55,974
And put this by your front door

357449
00:05:57,449 --> 00:05:59,256
This is a gadget that makes

359296
00:05:59,296 --> 00:06:00,949
The Halloween atmosphere even more lively

361294
00:06:01,294 --> 00:06:02,532
Once you turn it on

362573
00:06:02,573 --> 00:06:04,612
It creates an alternate space right there

364658
00:06:04,658 --> 00:06:07,138
And monsters will come greet whoever visits

378459
00:06:18,459 --> 00:06:19,510
Amazing!

379551
00:06:19,551 --> 00:06:22,888
-Gian probably won't dare go inside like this
-What's yours is mine

382929
00:06:22,929 --> 00:06:23,631
Here he comes!

385977
00:06:25,977 --> 00:06:28,333
-Let's hurry inside for now
-What's mine...

388374
00:06:28,374 --> 00:06:29,813
Halloween

389879
00:06:29,879 --> 00:06:31,747
Halloween

392192
00:06:32,192 --> 00:06:33,899
Halloween

396513
00:06:36,513 --> 00:06:39,415
Huh? Did Nobita's house get rebuilt?

405734
00:06:45,734 --> 00:06:47,712
Whoa, what is that?

407752
00:06:47,752 --> 00:06:49,984
Mummy

413982
00:06:53,982 --> 00:06:56,521
Wow, your costume looks so real!

416561
00:06:56,561 --> 00:06:57,946
Where did you buy that outfit?

417986
00:06:57,986 --> 00:06:58,860
Mummy

418901
00:06:58,901 --> 00:07:01,481
I'm going to dress up as a mummy next Halloween too!

421600
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,347
Let's go, my friend!

424576
00:07:04,576 --> 00:07:06,782
Fierce battle tournament

427348
00:07:07,348 --> 00:07:10,128
Give me your precious things, or I'll play a trick!

431050
00:07:11,050 --> 00:07:12,212
-Why?
-Why?

432253
00:07:12,253 --> 00:07:14,312
Mummy

434589
00:07:14,589 --> 00:07:15,842
-Here
-Here

436650
00:07:16,650 --> 00:07:17,786
Goodbye!

438132
00:07:18,132 --> 00:07:20,019
It doesn't seem to work at all

440059
00:07:20,059 --> 00:07:22,850
You didn't scare him at all, how is that going to work?

442891
00:07:22,891 --> 00:07:24,109
Mummy

445437
00:07:25,437 --> 00:07:26,210
Hey

446251
00:07:26,251 --> 00:07:28,087
I'm taking this with me too

448956
00:07:28,956 --> 00:07:30,667
He even took the jack-o'-lantern!

455667
00:07:35,667 --> 00:07:37,847
Grabbing you tight concrete

458880
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:40,800
Tottori concert

462006
00:07:42,006 --> 00:07:43,266
I'm taking this!

463320
00:07:43,320 --> 00:07:46,193
Why did you come to my house again?

467589
00:07:47,589 --> 00:07:49,248
What a great haul!

469462
00:07:49,462 --> 00:07:52,449
If only every day were Halloween!

475789
00:07:55,789 --> 00:07:57,669
This is way too much, completely ridiculous!

477709
00:07:57,709 --> 00:08:00,121
This is outright robbery!

481235
00:08:01,235 --> 00:08:03,675
We can't let Gian run wild anymore

483814
00:08:03,814 --> 00:08:05,731
We have to take back the things he took!

485771
00:08:05,771 --> 00:08:07,880
So, what should we do then?

487964
00:08:07,964 --> 00:08:09,449
Let's just go find Gian

489490
00:08:09,490 --> 00:08:11,391
And tell him "trick or treat!"

492730
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:15,329
How could we ever beat that robber?

495370
00:08:15,370 --> 00:08:16,864
Leave it to me!

498543
00:08:18,543 --> 00:08:20,273
"Real-Object Flashlight"

500847
00:08:20,847 --> 00:08:22,846
Shizuka, I want to shine the light on the broom

502928
00:08:22,928 --> 00:08:23,802
Sure

504748
00:08:24,748 --> 00:08:26,961
Just shine this flashlight on it

507601
00:08:27,601 --> 00:08:29,773
All right, try getting on the broom

511592
00:08:31,592 --> 00:08:32,419
Like this?

514518
00:08:34,518 --> 00:08:35,596
It's floating!

515637
00:08:35,637 --> 00:08:38,235
Just like a real magic broom!

518276
00:08:38,276 --> 00:08:40,994
Any object shone on by the Real-Object Flashlight

521035
00:08:41,035 --> 00:08:44,214
will definitely gain all the functions of the real thing

524313
00:08:44,313 --> 00:08:45,588
Awesome, I want one too!

525628
00:08:45,628 --> 00:08:47,108
Me too!

532935
00:08:52,935 --> 00:08:54,428
It doesn't hurt at all!

535367
00:08:55,367 --> 00:08:57,054
The arrows fly with real power!

537129
00:08:57,129 --> 00:08:59,069
I'm a king!

539622
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:00,428
Huh?

540568
00:09:00,568 --> 00:09:02,774
What can a king even do?

542977
00:09:02,977 --> 00:09:05,320
Alright, let's go find Gian

545458
00:09:05,458 --> 00:09:06,695
- Okay!
- Okay!

549339
00:09:09,339 --> 00:09:11,550
We've been everywhere already!

552980
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:15,317
Alright, let's go through them from the start again

559657
00:09:19,657 --> 00:09:21,217
This one doesn't work either

561257
00:09:21,257 --> 00:09:22,192
Gian!

565777
00:09:25,777 --> 00:09:26,914
Ready

567057
00:09:27,057 --> 00:09:28,976
- Trick or treat!
- Trick or treat!

569017
00:09:29,017 --> 00:09:32,082
Give us our stuff back or we'll play a trick!

574443
00:09:34,443 --> 00:09:35,987
That suits me just fine!

576197
00:09:36,197 --> 00:09:38,787
If you've got what it takes, just try me!

587882
00:09:47,882 --> 00:09:50,258
So it was one of Doraemon's gadgets?

595950
00:09:55,950 --> 00:09:56,980
Doraemon!

597020
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,149
Don't worry

598189
00:09:58,189 --> 00:10:00,705
We used the Real-Object Flashlight earlier, remember?

601028
00:10:01,028 --> 00:10:02,148
But it's so scary!

602188
00:10:02,188 --> 00:10:03,810
Are you really supposed to be a knight?

604547
00:10:04,547 --> 00:10:05,410
A knight?

605451
00:10:05,451 --> 00:10:07,463
I thought he was a samurai

607596
00:10:07,596 --> 00:10:08,750
Give me a break

608906
00:10:08,906 --> 00:10:11,370
I'm a knight! Charge!

615863
00:10:15,863 --> 00:10:17,983
Don't back down, fight!

626966
00:10:26,966 --> 00:10:28,786
Skeletons!

633299
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:34,316
Skeletons!

638721
00:10:38,721 --> 00:10:40,635
Skeletons...

640755
00:10:40,755 --> 00:10:41,995
Ouch!

644246
00:10:44,246 --> 00:10:45,862
You can't just hide!

646076
00:10:46,076 --> 00:10:48,398
But I'm the king right now!

648439
00:10:48,439 --> 00:10:51,081
Isn't it a minister's duty to protect the king?

651121
00:10:51,121 --> 00:10:52,744
Who's your minister?

652785
00:10:52,785 --> 00:10:54,071
Skeleton!

656832
00:10:56,832 --> 00:10:58,263
Not bad

658529
00:10:58,529 --> 00:11:00,832
In that case, take this!

667742
00:11:07,742 --> 00:11:09,421
There are so many?

669535
00:11:09,535 --> 00:11:10,990
We can't even count them all!

672397
00:11:12,397 --> 00:11:14,165
I've had enough!

676014
00:11:16,014 --> 00:11:17,666
Mummies!

681076
00:11:21,076 --> 00:11:23,562
Mommy!

692836
00:11:32,836 --> 00:11:34,423
Suneo, now's our chance!

694463
00:11:34,463 --> 00:11:36,289
Quick, put out the Jack-o'-Lanterns!

700552
00:11:40,552 --> 00:11:42,832
Hey, Suneo

703167
00:11:43,167 --> 00:11:45,918
Who's the real king, anyway?

707792
00:11:47,792 --> 00:11:49,146
The king...

710873
00:11:50,873 --> 00:11:52,879
Lord Gian, of course!

712920
00:11:52,920 --> 00:11:55,239
I am merely your humble minister

715805
00:11:55,805 --> 00:11:56,719
Not again

716759
00:11:56,759 --> 00:11:58,025
Betraying us again!

718215
00:11:58,215 --> 00:11:59,493
What should we do?

723638
00:12:03,638 --> 00:12:04,652
Oh no...

725192
00:12:05,192 --> 00:12:06,926
Shizuka, Dekisugi

729744
00:12:09,744 --> 00:12:11,143
Dekisugi

732343
00:12:12,343 --> 00:12:13,920
- Nobita
- Grab onto me!

735337
00:12:15,337 --> 00:12:16,780
Long live Halloween!

736821
00:12:16,821 --> 00:12:18,417
Long live Gian!

763033
00:12:43,033 --> 00:12:45,719
Halloween really is a dangerous holiday

767435
00:12:47,435 --> 00:12:49,759
Halloween isn't supposed to be like this

775865
00:12:55,865 --> 00:12:58,034
"Tasting Spoon"

780135
00:13:00,135 --> 00:13:03,075
Australian steak really does taste great

783440
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:06,434
And shark fin in Hong Kong is quite unforgettable too

786500
00:13:06,500 --> 00:13:08,527
In this world, there's nothing left

788568
00:13:08,568 --> 00:13:10,580
that I, Suneo, haven't eaten yet

790643
00:13:10,643 --> 00:13:13,204
So what's the most delicious thing you've ever eaten?

793245
00:13:13,245 --> 00:13:15,525
The best food is still the world's three greatest delicacies

795566
00:13:15,566 --> 00:13:17,891
Caviar, foie gras, and truffles

798025
00:13:18,025 --> 00:13:18,790
This is

798831
00:13:18,831 --> 00:13:21,945
caviar I had at a three-star restaurant in France

802450
00:13:22,450 --> 00:13:24,052
These black things?

804092
00:13:24,092 --> 00:13:26,141
Yes, that's right, they're sturgeon roe

806452
00:13:26,452 --> 00:13:28,493
Just one bite fills your mouth with flavor

808533
00:13:28,533 --> 00:13:31,710
This caviar is practically a gem of the sea

811751
00:13:31,751 --> 00:13:34,102
Wh-What is foie gras?

814255
00:13:34,255 --> 00:13:35,884
It's goose liver

815925
00:13:35,925 --> 00:13:38,471
Its rich flavor makes your mouth water

818512
00:13:38,512 --> 00:13:41,499
If you ever get the chance to go to France, you should try it too

823311
00:13:43,311 --> 00:13:45,099
Having experienced world-class cuisine

825139
00:13:45,139 --> 00:13:47,667
ordinary food just can't satisfy me anymore

827761
00:13:47,761 --> 00:13:51,087
But I'm sure you guys wouldn't
understand this kind of trouble

833699
00:13:53,699 --> 00:13:56,259
That Suneo is always showing off

836299
00:13:56,299 --> 00:13:58,334
The world's three greatest delicacies Suneo talked about

838381
00:13:58,381 --> 00:13:59,933
I wonder what they taste like?

840539
00:14:00,539 --> 00:14:02,433
I really want to try them

842779
00:14:02,779 --> 00:14:04,779
I'm home, what's for dinner?

844819
00:14:04,819 --> 00:14:06,116
Dried horse mackerel

847277
00:14:07,277 --> 00:14:09,964
I really want to eat caviar, one of the world's three greatest delicacies

850004
00:14:10,004 --> 00:14:12,281
or something like foie gras!

853141
00:14:13,141 --> 00:14:14,861
Caviar is just expensive

854901
00:14:14,901 --> 00:14:16,577
It's not even particularly tasty

856630
00:14:16,630 --> 00:14:18,569
Pollock roe is way tastier

858683
00:14:18,683 --> 00:14:19,922
Pollock roe?

862708
00:14:22,708 --> 00:14:24,308
Thanks for the food

873955
00:14:33,955 --> 00:14:35,669
Delicious!

876548
00:14:36,548 --> 00:14:37,848
What is that?

877953
00:14:37,953 --> 00:14:40,314
It's called the Tasting Spoon

880428
00:14:40,428 --> 00:14:43,840
It's a spoon that lets you taste
food shown in photos

883881
00:14:43,881 --> 00:14:45,088
Lend it to me!

889288
00:14:49,288 --> 00:14:50,530
Why didn't it work?

892245
00:14:52,245 --> 00:14:53,543
Because it's only for tasting

893584
00:14:53,584 --> 00:14:56,197
so each photo can only be tasted once

896238
00:14:56,238 --> 00:14:57,249
Really?

897296
00:14:57,296 --> 00:14:58,130
But

898396
00:14:58,396 --> 00:14:59,823
if you switch to another photo

900253
00:15:00,253 --> 00:15:03,182
or use another spoon, it'll work fine

903236
00:15:03,236 --> 00:15:04,150
Here

904384
00:15:04,384 --> 00:15:06,097
Wow, awesome!

908802
00:15:08,802 --> 00:15:10,221
Thanks for the food

913397
00:15:13,397 --> 00:15:14,650
Delicious

914944
00:15:14,944 --> 00:15:15,910
Right

915951
00:15:15,951 --> 00:15:17,144
Here, Shizuka

917363
00:15:17,363 --> 00:15:18,684
Thank you

919342
00:15:19,342 --> 00:15:20,389
That's so neat!

920430
00:15:20,430 --> 00:15:21,919
So with this, we can eat

921959
00:15:21,959 --> 00:15:23,598
the world's three greatest delicacies?

924378
00:15:24,378 --> 00:15:26,403
But I don't really want to go to Suneo

926444
00:15:26,444 --> 00:15:28,239
and ask him to show us his photos

928375
00:15:28,375 --> 00:15:31,472
We should be able to find some at the bookstore in the shopping street

931854
00:15:31,854 --> 00:15:34,167
-That's our...
-That's our Shizuka!

939993
00:15:39,993 --> 00:15:42,150
Excuse me, what is this line for?

942197
00:15:42,197 --> 00:15:43,024
Ramen

943117
00:15:43,117 --> 00:15:44,504
It was featured in a magazine

944632
00:15:44,632 --> 00:15:46,744
Look, doesn't it look delicious?

947152
00:15:47,152 --> 00:15:48,432
It looks so good!

948472
00:15:48,472 --> 00:15:49,752
I really want to try it

949792
00:15:49,792 --> 00:15:52,238
Could we borrow your magazine for a look?

962461
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:05,201
Even though it looked delicious in the photo...

965750
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:07,814
it's not good enough to wait in a long line for

968591
00:16:08,591 --> 00:16:10,961
Just looking at it makes my stomach rumble

971391
00:16:11,391 --> 00:16:12,777
Oh, Nobita, honestly...

973924
00:16:13,924 --> 00:16:16,377
Where are the world's three greatest delicacies?

976904
00:16:16,904 --> 00:16:18,503
Caviar...

978570
00:16:18,570 --> 00:16:20,163
"Everything You Love About the Okonomiyaki
Everyone's Talking About"

981192
00:16:21,192 --> 00:16:23,445
What delicious-looking okonomiyaki!

987232
00:16:27,232 --> 00:16:28,405
Delicious!

988887
00:16:28,887 --> 00:16:31,041
I've wanted to try this for so long!

991082
00:16:31,082 --> 00:16:33,373
Dorayaki from that famous shop

995127
00:16:35,127 --> 00:16:36,499
-Delicious!
-Delicious!

996630
00:16:36,630 --> 00:16:39,519
I've got to find something to taste too

1000802
00:16:40,802 --> 00:16:42,181
No browsing without buying!

1002222
00:16:42,222 --> 00:16:44,955
No, I'm not reading, I'm eating!

1005882
00:16:45,882 --> 00:16:47,282
Get out of here!

1012104
00:16:52,104 --> 00:16:54,405
Sigh, and I thought we'd get to try

1014445
00:16:54,445 --> 00:16:56,671
all of the world's three greatest delicacies at once

1016876
00:16:56,876 --> 00:16:59,478
Is there anywhere else we can find photos?

1019677
00:16:59,677 --> 00:17:01,080
Well, we have no choice

1021121
00:17:01,121 --> 00:17:03,264
Why don't we just go to Suneo's house now?

1023364
00:17:03,364 --> 00:17:05,250
-Suneo!
-Suneo!

1025904
00:17:05,904 --> 00:17:06,870
What is it?

1027829
00:17:07,829 --> 00:17:09,861
Well, we came because we want to see

1029901
00:17:09,901 --> 00:17:12,394
your "World Gourmet Photo Album" again, Suneo

1032670
00:17:12,670 --> 00:17:14,160
You want to look at photos?

1034201
00:17:14,201 --> 00:17:17,124
I really want to hear more of your gourmet memories

1039311
00:17:19,311 --> 00:17:21,305
The most delicious caviar

1041345
00:17:21,345 --> 00:17:22,531
has to be this one

1042572
00:17:22,572 --> 00:17:25,637
I had it at a three-star restaurant in France

1047645
00:17:27,645 --> 00:17:28,652
All right then

1053377
00:17:33,377 --> 00:17:34,316
What?

1057942
00:17:37,942 --> 00:17:39,694
Wow, it's my first time seeing it

1059734
00:17:39,734 --> 00:17:41,654
It looks just like frog eggs!

1062114
00:17:42,114 --> 00:17:43,798
Fr... Frog eggs?

1069886
00:17:49,886 --> 00:17:51,400
It's certainly springy

1071493
00:17:51,493 --> 00:17:53,540
The texture is truly amazing

1073598
00:17:53,598 --> 00:17:55,850
It really is quite chewy

1075891
00:17:55,891 --> 00:17:57,643
It tastes pretty salty though

1077717
00:17:57,717 --> 00:18:00,302
If that's the case, pollock roe tastes better

1080409
00:18:00,409 --> 00:18:01,968
Suddenly I'm craving steaming hot

1082008
00:18:02,008 --> 00:18:03,688
white rice with pollock roe

1084276
00:18:04,276 --> 00:18:05,754
Huh, pollock roe?

1086157
00:18:06,157 --> 00:18:06,998
Then...

1087038
00:18:07,038 --> 00:18:08,310
Uh... what about foie gras?

1088351
00:18:08,351 --> 00:18:10,891
It's a top-class dish even the President of France has eaten

1095370
00:18:15,370 --> 00:18:17,043
It kind of looks like something

1098684
00:18:18,684 --> 00:18:21,283
I've got it, it's monkfish liver!

1102924
00:18:22,924 --> 00:18:25,377
My dad has eaten monkfish liver too

1105435
00:18:25,435 --> 00:18:26,156
Hey, Suneo

1106196
00:18:26,196 --> 00:18:27,670
Do you have photos of monkfish liver

1107710
00:18:27,710 --> 00:18:29,478
from a three-star restaurant too?

1109518
00:18:29,518 --> 00:18:31,089
How could I possibly have that?

1111160
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,263
Then what about truffles?

1112303
00:18:32,303 --> 00:18:34,916
It's top-grade stuff worth hundreds of thousands of yen!

1118108
00:18:38,108 --> 00:18:39,395
Doesn't it smell amazing?

1120854
00:18:40,854 --> 00:18:42,854
It doesn't seem to have much flavor

1123560
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:46,073
And here I thought it would be delicious

1127911
00:18:47,911 --> 00:18:50,372
The world's three great delicacies are nothing special

1130412
00:18:50,412 --> 00:18:51,618
Nothing special at all

1134077
00:18:54,077 --> 00:18:56,615
You guys don't appreciate how precious truffles are at all!

1136708
00:18:56,708 --> 00:18:58,180
Because they're so hard to find

1138220
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:01,010
people rely on specially trained dogs and pigs to find them!

1141051
00:19:01,051 --> 00:19:03,355
So they're food for dogs and pigs?

1143465
00:19:03,465 --> 00:19:04,785
What?!

1145028
00:19:05,028 --> 00:19:07,030
And here I thought we were in for a treat, what a disappointment

1147070
00:19:07,070 --> 00:19:09,946
How could you guys possibly understand world-class flavor?

1150104
00:19:10,104 --> 00:19:12,365
Get out of here!

1153491
00:19:13,491 --> 00:19:15,002
Well then, see you later

1155112
00:19:15,112 --> 00:19:16,564
- Bye
- Bye

1157512
00:19:17,512 --> 00:19:20,443
That Suneo is really infuriating, though

1160563
00:19:20,563 --> 00:19:21,475
In that case

1161516
00:19:21,516 --> 00:19:24,282
let's find some food Suneo's never eaten and give it to him!

1164992
00:19:24,992 --> 00:19:27,605
Where are we going to find something like that?

1167872
00:19:27,872 --> 00:19:29,186
No, not this

1169232
00:19:29,232 --> 00:19:32,037
Right, weren't you looking for canned mackerel?

1172439
00:19:32,439 --> 00:19:34,038
This is such a headache

1175826
00:19:35,826 --> 00:19:37,300
Mom, what's wrong?

1177340
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:38,779
That foreign customer over there...

1178819
00:19:38,819 --> 00:19:40,858
I don't understand what he wants at all

1180898
00:19:40,898 --> 00:19:42,217
So I'm really stuck

1182258
00:19:42,258 --> 00:19:45,212
I came all this way to find a taste of home

1185297
00:19:45,297 --> 00:19:46,818
A taste of home?

1186896
00:19:46,896 --> 00:19:49,374
Yes, I'm looking for some canned fish

1189415
00:19:49,415 --> 00:19:51,301
I came to Japan from Sweden

1191455
00:19:51,455 --> 00:19:52,821
Then is it this one?

1193660
00:19:53,660 --> 00:19:55,103
No, not this kind

1195144
00:19:55,144 --> 00:19:57,833
It's not? Then we probably don't have it here

1197932
00:19:57,932 --> 00:19:59,382
Then what should I do?

1199452
00:19:59,452 --> 00:20:02,156
Even just one bite, I really want to taste it

1203973
00:20:03,973 --> 00:20:06,094
I have an idea, do you have a photo?

1206134
00:20:06,134 --> 00:20:07,202
A photo?

1207695
00:20:07,695 --> 00:20:10,175
A photo of you eating that canned food before

1210216
00:20:10,216 --> 00:20:12,202
Oh, yes... I have one!

1212416
00:20:12,416 --> 00:20:14,707
Nobita, you're pretty sharp this time!

1214923
00:20:14,923 --> 00:20:16,017
Here it is

1217379
00:20:17,379 --> 00:20:19,388
It looks like canned saury

1219760
00:20:19,760 --> 00:20:21,705
- Looks delicious
- Here, use this

1222460
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:25,604
With this, you can taste the food in the photo once

1225951
00:20:25,951 --> 00:20:27,022
Use this?

1227063
00:20:27,063 --> 00:20:29,713
You'll see once you try it, go ahead and give it a shot

1229754
00:20:29,754 --> 00:20:30,884
Oh, okay

1240063
00:20:40,063 --> 00:20:41,814
What an overpowering smell!

1248389
00:20:48,389 --> 00:20:50,233
What a nostalgic smell

1251181
00:20:51,181 --> 00:20:53,967
This is 100% the taste of home!

1254029
00:20:54,029 --> 00:20:57,560
People from different countries have such different tastes

1262593
00:21:02,593 --> 00:21:05,039
"Universal Encyclopedia"

1265852
00:21:05,852 --> 00:21:07,259
What would you like to search for?

1267330
00:21:07,330 --> 00:21:09,723
Strong-smelling canned food from Sweden

1270145
00:21:10,145 --> 00:21:11,942
This canned food is intense

1272861
00:21:12,861 --> 00:21:15,216
Turns out it's surströmming

1275257
00:21:15,257 --> 00:21:18,140
Canned herring fermented in Sweden

1278180
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:20,424
Known as the smelliest food in the world

1280465
00:21:20,465 --> 00:21:21,448
Number one in the world?

1281488
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:22,568
No wonder!

1282648
00:21:22,648 --> 00:21:24,601
I brought some new photos

1284729
00:21:24,729 --> 00:21:26,347
Because I felt sorry that you all can only

1286387
00:21:26,387 --> 00:21:29,823
use such a tiny spoon to find food, it's just so pitiful

1293610
00:21:33,610 --> 00:21:35,452
By the way, Suneo, didn't you say

1295493
00:21:35,493 --> 00:21:37,980
there's nothing in the world you haven't eaten?

1298020
00:21:38,020 --> 00:21:39,859
Well, of course!

1299900
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:41,043
I'm very different from you guys

1301084
00:21:41,084 --> 00:21:43,831
After all, I've traveled all over the world

1304006
00:21:44,006 --> 00:21:45,123
All right

1305805
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:47,398
Do you know what this is?

1308293
00:21:48,293 --> 00:21:49,680
You really don't know?

1310101
00:21:50,101 --> 00:21:52,541
Didn't you say you've traveled all over the world?

1314273
00:21:54,273 --> 00:21:56,374
This thing? Of course I know!

1316554
00:21:56,554 --> 00:21:57,687
I remember it's called...

1317727
00:21:57,727 --> 00:21:59,280
Surströmming

1319321
00:21:59,321 --> 00:22:00,737
Ah, yes, that's right, exactly...

1320777
00:22:00,777 --> 00:22:03,160
You know it quite well, Doraemon

1323306
00:22:03,306 --> 00:22:05,214
So is it from Switzerland?

1325254
00:22:05,254 --> 00:22:07,326
Yeah, exactly, Switzerland, Switzerland!

1327645
00:22:07,645 --> 00:22:10,565
I ate it when climbing the Matterhorn

1330606
00:22:10,606 --> 00:22:12,669
Not Switzerland, it should be Sweden

1332876
00:22:12,876 --> 00:22:14,156
Oh, is it?

1334196
00:22:14,196 --> 00:22:15,755
Right, I remember now

1335796
00:22:15,796 --> 00:22:17,332
It wasn't on the Matterhorn

1337373
00:22:17,373 --> 00:22:20,280
It was when I was watching the Northern Lights

1340500
00:22:20,500 --> 00:22:22,182
So, what does it taste like?

1343174
00:22:23,174 --> 00:22:25,153
Well, with just one bite

1345194
00:22:25,194 --> 00:22:26,681
a heavenly, delicious aroma

1346721
00:22:26,721 --> 00:22:29,084
immediately filled my entire mouth!

1349125
00:22:29,125 --> 00:22:30,685
In that case, want to try some?

1357217
00:22:37,217 --> 00:22:40,083
Actually, I've really missed that flavor

1360160
00:22:40,160 --> 00:22:41,536
Just looking at the photo

1361576
00:22:41,576 --> 00:22:43,789
I can already smell the fragrance

1363864
00:22:43,864 --> 00:22:46,796
It'd be such a pity to only have one bite

1366837
00:22:46,837 --> 00:22:49,438
Then go ahead and eat a whole big spoonful!

1370456
00:22:50,456 --> 00:22:53,480
Uh, well then, don't mind if I do

1378986
00:22:58,986 --> 00:23:00,426
What's wrong?

1382287
00:23:02,287 --> 00:23:04,005
What is this smell?

1384328
00:23:04,328 --> 00:23:07,053
You said it was a heavenly, delicious aroma

1387094
00:23:07,094 --> 00:23:09,028
What's the matter? Aren't you going to eat it?

1389806
00:23:09,806 --> 00:23:13,258
Usually, you have to smell it thoroughly first

1395507
00:23:15,507 --> 00:23:18,349
I think I'll take it home to savor it

1398577
00:23:18,577 --> 00:23:21,336
Because I want to share some with my mom

1401720
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,226
Don't be polite!

1403267
00:23:23,267 --> 00:23:26,539
We really want to see you enjoy it, Suneo!

1406886
00:23:26,886 --> 00:23:28,360
Really?

1408763
00:23:28,763 --> 00:23:30,111
Then...

1415622
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:37,187
It's... it's moving!

1417227
00:23:37,227 --> 00:23:38,312
Amazing!

1418353
00:23:38,353 --> 00:23:39,942
Is it delicious? Really?

1419982
00:23:39,982 --> 00:23:42,294
He really understands world-class cuisine

1422335
00:23:42,335 --> 00:23:44,511
He really is so different from us

1424552
00:23:44,552 --> 00:23:48,130
Of course, I'm on a completely different level from you guys

1428418
00:23:48,418 --> 00:23:49,461
But you know

1429501
00:23:49,501 --> 00:23:52,140
Just one bite isn't enough to really taste it, right?

1432599
00:23:52,599 --> 00:23:53,606
I want that one first

1433646
00:23:53,646 --> 00:23:56,599
Oh, I have plenty of that right here

1436791
00:23:56,791 --> 00:23:59,209
Here, help yourself!

1440865
00:24:00,865 --> 00:24:03,827
Swe... Swedish surströmming

1444047
00:24:04,047 --> 00:24:07,217
One bite of this is more than enough!

1450119
00:24:10,119 --> 00:24:11,659
-Suneo...
-Suneo...

1451699
00:24:11,699 --> 00:24:13,815
-Hang in there!
-Hey, Suneo!

1453994
00:24:13,994 --> 00:24:15,521
Sha-la-la-la-la

1455581
00:24:15,581 --> 00:24:18,020
Sing along with me

1458107
00:24:18,107 --> 00:24:19,460
Shouting out for an encore

1459514
00:24:19,514 --> 00:24:21,948
Marching along together in joy

1462127
00:24:22,127 --> 00:24:23,340
Doraemon

1463395
00:24:23,395 --> 00:24:25,374
Making this moment timeless

1465407
00:24:25,407 --> 00:24:31,784
Beautiful sights will come into view

